    ('common', "current_reference is the current user's explicit object reference; respect its current_geometry flag. latest_user_reply preserves the original question and human reply even after history trimming. Interpret that reply in its original context; a completed confirmation remains valid until the user changes the decision. latest_observation and latest_failure are mandatory execution observations. A truncated observation is an excerpt: expand it using read_tool_result before relying on missing details. context_omissions reports omitted historical entries; their absence does not mean earlier work did not happen. Failed actions are evidence of failure, never of a constructed model. Use their actual errors to correct recoverable scripts."),
